      },
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the original number of students. The original number of boys is $0.55n$. After five boys join, there are $0.55n+5$ boys and $n+5$ students.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{0.55n+5}{n+5}&=0.64\\\\0.55n+5&=0.64(n+5)\\\\55n+500&=64(n+5)\\\\55n+500&=64n+320\\\\180&=9n\\\\n&=\\frac{180}{9}\\\\n&=20\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere were originally 20 students. Check: 11 boys become 16 boys out of 25 students, and $\\frac{16}{25}\\times100\\%=64\\%$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 96
